In a production microservices architecture, an API Gateway is the single entry point for all client requests. Instead of calling each service directly, clients send requests to the gateway, which routes them to the correct service.

In the Spring ecosystem, the most common gateway is Spring Cloud Gateway. It works very well with Netflix Eureka and centralized configuration using Spring Cloud Config.

