1️⃣ JWT Authentication Implementation in Gateway

In most fintech systems, authentication is handled at the gateway layer instead of every service.

JWT usually comes from an Auth Service.

Flow:

Client Login
     ↓
Auth Service
     ↓
JWT Token Generated
     ↓
Client sends JWT in Header
     ↓
API Gateway validates token
     ↓
Forward request to microservice

Token header example:

Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9
Gateway Filter Example

Create a filter to validate JWT.

@Component
public class JwtAuthenticationFilter implements GlobalFilter {

    @Override
    public Mono<Void> filter(ServerWebExchange exchange,
                             GatewayFilterChain chain) {

        String authHeader = exchange.getRequest()
                .getHeaders()
                .getFirst("Authorization");

        if (authHeader == null || !authHeader.startsWith("Bearer ")) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Missing token");
        }

        String token = authHeader.substring(7);

        if (!JwtUtil.validateToken(token)) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Invalid JWT");
        }

        return chain.filter(exchange);
    }
}

Responsibilities:

Extract JWT

Validate signature

Validate expiration

Forward request

2️⃣ Rate Limiter Implementation

Rate limiting protects APIs from abuse.

Example:

100 requests per minute per user

Gateway supports Redis-based rate limiting using Redis.

Example Configuration
spring:
  cloud:
    gateway:
      routes:
        - id: account-service
          uri: lb://ACCOUNT-SERVICE
          predicates:
            - Path=/accounts/**
          filters:
            - name: RequestRateLimiter
              args:
                redis-rate-limiter.replenishRate: 10
                redis-rate-limiter.burstCapacity: 20

Meaning:

10 requests per second
burst up to 20
Rate Limiting Flow
Client Request
     ↓
Gateway
     ↓
Check Redis Counter
     ↓
If limit exceeded → Reject request

Response:

HTTP 429 TOO MANY REQUESTS
3️⃣ Gateway Filter Coding Questions

Interviewers often ask:

Write a custom filter to log requests.

Example:

@Component
public class LoggingFilter implements GlobalFilter {

    @Override
    public Mono<Void> filter(ServerWebExchange exchange,
                             GatewayFilterChain chain) {

        ServerHttpRequest request = exchange.getRequest();

        System.out.println("Request Path: " + request.getURI());
        System.out.println("Method: " + request.getMethod());

        return chain.filter(exchange);
    }
}
